  <scopecontent id="aspace_62369301cdf22c5059fc6eddd63cca21">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>This collection consists of 358 color photographs taken by arts administrator, curator, and artist Paul J. Smith (1931-2020). The photos document various parades and events that took place in New York City between 1996 and 2016. Included are images of the Easter Parade on Fifth Avenue, the Mermaid Parade in Coney Island, the West Indian Day Parade in Brooklyn, and the Halloween Dog Parade in Tompkins Square Park. There are also photos of Wigstock, the Howl! Festival, a Save Our Gardens event, the Gates art installation in Central Park, and Santa Con, as well as photos of tattoos and art in Coney Island. A small amount of ephemera can be found in the collection, including printouts of websites.</p>  </scopecontent>
